  "notes": "MUSIC TERM:\nハーモニー is used extensively in music to describe the combination of different notes or voices. It's also used metaphorically for any pleasing combination.\n\nMUSIC COLLOCATIONS:\n- ハーモニーを{合|あ}わせる - to match harmonies\n- {美|うつく}しいハーモニー - beautiful harmony\n- ハーモニーが{崩|くず}れる - harmony breaks down\n- {三|さん}{部|ぶ}/{四|よん}{部|ぶ}ハーモニー - three-part/four-part harmony\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {和音|わおん} - chord (technical music term)\n- {調和|ちょうわ} - harmony, balance (general/formal)\n- メロディー - melody\n- コーラス - chorus\n\nUSAGE:\n{調和|ちょうわ} is the native Japanese word for harmony (balance/coordination), while ハーモニー is specifically used in musical contexts or for aesthetic combinations.",
